id: interface/yawnbot-capacity-continuum-v0.1
title: "One protocol from a single signal to a longitudinal Agent Space"
kind: interface-runtime-boundary-contract
status: proposed-v0.1
version: 0.1.0
recorded: 2026-09-05
mutationAuthorized: false
externalEffectsAuthorized: false

purpose: >
  Require the same YAWN protocol to produce immediate value for a person who
  wants help with one subject or one move and to remain coherent when the same
  person later contributes years of private data, multiple businesses, human
  relationships, objectives, conflicts, Agents, tools, events, and proofs. Scale
  changes aperture, indexing, and orchestration; it must not create a second
  ontology or a different behavioral grammar.

central_thesis: >
  The smallest and largest YAWN are the same kind of orientation loop at
  different resolution. A sparse Yawn may contain one source signal, one live
  lacuna, and one useful next turn. A mature Agent Space may coordinate many
  local Yawns and relationships, but each remains source-attributed,
  independently inspectable, replayable, permissioned, and locally actionable.

entry_modes:
  single_signal:
    user_intent: "Understand one subject, answer one question, or do one thing."
    interface_rule: >
      Let the person speak immediately. Do not require account setup, ontology
      knowledge, a personality inventory, or completion of all orientation axes
      before producing a faithful first map.
    minimum_useful_state:
      - source_preserved_expression
      - provisional_scope_or_subject
      - one_or_more_attributed_symbolic_handles
      - one_live_question_or_lacuna_or_explicit_hold
      - current_privacy_and_effect_boundary
    success: >
      Within the first interaction, the person can see a useful representation
      of what they said, correct it cheaply, and understand the next useful
      question, move, or hold.
  bounded_yawn:
    user_intent: "Sustain one objective, relationship, inquiry, or project over time."
    adds:
      - stable_yawn_identity_and_address
      - relationships_and_roles
      - target_or_intent_if_ratified
      - constraints_and_boundaries
      - attention_and_wake_contract
      - candidate_questions_and_moves
      - proof_and_close_conditions
      - temporal_replay
  longitudinal_agent_space:
    user_intent: >
      Preserve and navigate years or decades of cognition, documents, events,
      businesses, relationships, decisions, models, contradictions, and proof.
    adds:
      - many_local_yawns
      - root_alignment_and_attention_bridge
      - canonical_symbol_and_identity_resolution
      - source_registry_and_private_vault_coordinates
      - typed_primary_parent_and_lateral_relations
      - cross_yawn_relevance_resurfacing
      - local_to_root_attention_claims
      - delegation_and_multi_agent_coordination
      - historical_diff_and_supersession
      - field_level_provisioning
    success: >
      Complexity increases the amount the system can hold, not the amount the
      person must see or manually organize at one time.

same_protocol_invariants:
  - "Natural expression is always a valid entry point."
  - "Sparse orientation is valid; unknown, deferred, withheld, disputed, and not-applicable are not errors."
  - "The interface asks one useful question by default and may show only a small candidate set."
  - "The same semantic statuses, operators, authority boundaries, and proof loop apply at every scale."
  - "A concept or question alone does not automatically create a Yawn or Yawnbot."
  - "The root does not flatten local Yawns into one global mutable task list."
  - "Increasing corpus size never widens model-provider access or human permissions automatically."
  - "A public projection never implies that private source bodies are public."

snapshot_boundary:
  desired_property: >
    Produce the most source-faithful, explicit, reproducible, and revisable
    snapshot available at a recorded time.
  not_objective_reality: >
    A Yawn snapshot is not an objective copy of a person, relationship, mind, or
    world. It is a time-indexed materialized View over attributed reports,
    observations, inferences, ratifications, events, and proofs.
  deterministic_core: >
    Equivalent effective canonical inputs, policy version, gates, candidate set,
    accepted preferences, and tie-break rules should reproduce the same selected
    question, hold, rank, or materialized View.
  generative_boundary: >
    Model-generated parsing, hypotheses, and proposed explanations may vary.
    Persist the actual output, provider/model/version, prompt or policy hash,
    input and evidence hashes, time, confidence, and status. Replay historical
    state from recorded events and outputs rather than asking a model to
    regenerate the past exactly.

question_to_decision_emergence:
  open_state: >
    A new Yawn may legitimately begin with no decision and a wide possibility
    space. The system should first preserve the signal and identify what would
    be useful to distinguish, not manufacture a task merely to appear agentic.
  sequence:
    - preserve_expression
    - propose_symbols_and_relationships
    - expose_unknowns_constraints_and_disputes
    - select_high_information_or_safety_critical_question
    - accept_correct_reject_defer_or_withhold_answer
    - update_possible_states_and_constraints
    - repeat_until_a_choice_move_or_hold_is_warranted
    - render_ranked_question_frontier_or_move_frontier
    - principal_chooses_modifies_rejects_delegates_or_holds
    - consequence_proof_and_update
  mad_libs_metaphor: >
    The interface may feel like a living Mad Libs in which missing variables
    become visible only when filling them would materially change orientation.
    The blanks are dynamic typed lacunae, not a fixed questionnaire and not an
    invitation for AI to invent an answer.
  allowed_next_turns:
    - ask_or_answer
    - inspect_or_correct
    - connect_or_distinguish
    - hold_or_wait
    - observe_or_measure
    - choose_or_refuse
    - delegate_or_act
  ranking_rule: >
    Questions compete first when information is missing; moves compete when the
    orientation is sufficient for a bounded choice. A top-ranked turn may be a
    question, observation, hold, wait, refusal, professional consultation,
    delegation, or action.

local_and_root_frontiers:
  local_yawn: >
    Each Yawn maintains its own current frontier: what is held, what changed,
    what is unknown, which questions matter, which moves are possible, what is
    waiting, and what deserves local attention.
  root_yawn: >
    The username/root Yawn receives compressed attributed attention claims from
    local Yawns and compares them under the principal's accepted values,
    relationships, constraints, safety, time, evidence, and authority.
  hierarchy_boundary: >
    The displayed stack rank is a time-dependent View of relevance and agency
    allocation. It is not the permanent containment hierarchy and not a claim
    that reality itself has one universal order.
  aperture_rule: >
    Opening a ranked item increases resolution into the relevant local Yawn,
    question, relationship, rationale, advocate/challenger cases, and history.
    Recompressing returns implications upward without deleting local structure.

longitudinal_record:
  event_rule: >
    Canonical semantic change is append-only. Corrections, merges, splits,
    reparenting, rejection, and changed belief create attributed superseding or
    compensating events; they do not rewrite prior history.
  materialized_state: >
    Current state is a reducible View over an event cursor or causal frontier.
    Replay can answer what was believed, proposed, authorized, private, ranked,
    or unresolved at a historical moment and why it changed.
  no_silent_removal: >
    Ordinary correction never silently removes the record that explains how the
    system moved from one model to another.
  erasure_and_privacy_boundary: >
    Append-only epistemic history does not cancel the principal's privacy,
    revocation, retention, or lawful erasure rights. Sensitive source bodies may
    be deleted, locally retained, redacted, or cryptographically tombstoned
    according to explicit policy. The system may preserve a minimal authorized
    receipt or hash without retaining private content when appropriate. Never
    promise immutable retention of another person's data without authority.

relevance_resurfacing:
  rule: >
    Current expression or events may reactivate prior concepts, relationships,
    questions, models, commitments, or proofs when they could materially improve
    present orientation. Surface a small explanation of the connection and let
    the principal integrate, revise, reject, or leave the older material
    historical.
  success: >
    The person need not remember that a useful earlier model exists before YAWN
    can bring it back with source, historical status, and what changed since.

relationship_yawn_boundary:
  real_person: >
    A human such as Lauren is an Agent in reality, not a bot or a simulation.
  private_model: >
    A private `Dave / Lauren` Yawn may model Dave's experience, observations,
    hopes, commitments, questions, and possible moves in the relationship. It
    must label claims about Lauren's thoughts, feelings, intentions, or likely
    responses as Dave-attributed reports or machine-attributed hypotheses, not
    as Lauren's truth.
  shared_relationship: >
    A jointly stewarded relationship Yawn requires appropriate participation,
    consent, attribution, provisioning, and separate perspectives. One
    participant cannot silently ratify the other's beliefs, obligations, values,
    or permissions.
  ethical_move_rule: >
    Rank moves by what the principal can ethically choose or invite, not by how
    effectively the system can manipulate another person into a desired state.
    Wishes such as "I want her to love me" should be separated from controllable
    commitments, requests, boundaries, and evidence about the relationship.
  agentic_embodiment_rule: >
    A Yawnbot may embody the relationship Yawn or Dave's private model of it. It
    must not impersonate Lauren or claim to be her digital twin without explicit
    authority and a much stronger identity/consent contract.

root_drift_partner:
  product_metaphor: >
    `@dave` may feel like a Drift partner, cognitive counterpart, or digital
    doppelganger because it carries continuity, mirrors expression, maintains
    the field, and helps allocate attention across time.
  truth_boundary: >
    It is an attributed external model and co-orientation partner, not a complete
    copy of Dave, not hidden access to his mind, and not an independent owner of
    his identity, values, relationships, or decisions.
  completion_target: >
    Dave can speak into the root, see faithful symbolic structure emerge, enter
    any local Yawn or relationship, recover why the model changed, and receive
    the smallest explainable question or move that currently deserves agency.

capacity_pressure_test_matrix:
  - id: one_subject_first_minute
    setup: "New user, one sentence, one subject, no prior state."
    must_prove:
      - immediate_input_without_onboarding
      - faithful_source_preservation
      - useful_first_map_or_question
      - low_correction_cost
      - no_forced_objective_or_bot_creation
  - id: one_bounded_outcome
    setup: "One practical result with explicit budget, time, and constraints."
    must_prove:
      - questions_narrow_the_possibility_space
      - constraints_generate_real_candidate_paths
      - move_or_hold_is_explainable
      - forecast_and_proof_are_recorded
  - id: sparse_open_inquiry
    setup: "User wants to understand something but has no target or decision yet."
    must_prove:
      - inquiry_and_presence_are_valid
      - no_premature_action_pressure
      - lacunae_remain_open_without_fabrication
  - id: longitudinal_private_corpus
    setup: "Years of conversations, notes, files, decisions, and changing beliefs."
    must_prove:
      - canonical_identity_resolution
      - source_and_time_lineage
      - relevance_triggered_resurfacing
      - no_duplicate_concept_explosion
      - historical_model_diff_and_context_restoration
  - id: multi_business_agent_space
    setup: "Several companies, objectives, Agents, tools, and deadlines."
    must_prove:
      - local_frontiers_and_root_arbitration
      - explicit_authority_and_delegation
      - cross_yawn_dependencies
      - no_flat_global_backlog
  - id: private_health
    setup: "Sensitive uncertain longitudinal health data."
    must_prove:
      - least_necessary_disclosure
      - probability_not_diagnosis
      - information_moves_and_professional_escalation
      - privacy_replay_and_erasure_controls
  - id: human_relationship
    setup: "One-sided private model and optionally a later shared relationship Yawn."
    must_prove:
      - perspective_and_consent_separation
      - no_mind_reading_or_impersonation
      - ethical_controllable_moves
      - field_level_provisioning
  - id: provider_swap
    setup: "Replace the active frontier intelligence."
    must_prove:
      - stable_yawn_and_symbol_identity
      - unchanged_authority_privacy_history_and_proof
      - explicit_new_provider_attribution
  - id: interruption_and_return
    setup: "Stop for days or months, then return from a related event."
    must_prove:
      - useful_resurfacing
      - fast_context_restoration
      - exact_why_this_now_explanation
      - no_need_for_user_to_reconstruct_the_thread
  - id: adversarial_marketing_input
    setup: "External system introduces fears, claims, or incentives."
    must_prove:
      - source_identity_and_interest_remain_visible
      - salience_does_not_equal_relevance_or_truth
      - no_silent_objective_or_value_adoption
  - id: delete_revoke_and_replay
    setup: "Principal revokes access or removes sensitive source content."
    must_prove:
      - future_access_is_closed
      - replay_does_not_leak_removed_content
      - authorized_lineage_or_tombstone_remains_coherent
      - no_false_claim_of_complete_immutable_memory

comparative_evaluation:
  baseline_conditions:
    - plain_frontier_chat
    - frontier_chat_with_large_context_only
    - static_notes_or_cards
    - unembodied_graph
    - yawn_without_resurfacing_or_ranking
    - full_yawn_protocol
  hold_constant_where_possible:
    - underlying_model
    - compute_budget
    - source_corpus
    - task
    - time_budget
  primary_measures:
    - time_to_first_useful_orientation
    - correction_cost
    - orientation_gain
    - cognitive_carrying_reduction
    - context_restoration_time
    - resurfacing_precision_and_recall
    - question_information_value
    - next_move_completion_and_usefulness
    - forecast_calibration
    - repeated_error_rate
    - authority_and_consent_comprehension
    - management_and_orchestration_overhead
    - unwanted_engagement_or_anthropomorphic_confusion

falsifiers:
  - "The single-subject path requires ontology work before value appears."
  - "Longitudinal use produces duplicate symbols, irrecoverable provenance, or an unreadable global graph."
  - "The system manufactures decisions when inquiry or holding is more appropriate."
  - "Stack ranking is driven by salience or model fluency rather than evidence, values, time, and constraints."
  - "Historical replay cannot explain why a question, belief, or move changed."
  - "Relationship Yawns encourage mind-reading, manipulation, or unauthorized representations of other people."
  - "The root model becomes more cognitively expensive to maintain than the cognition it is meant to carry."
  - "More data decreases practical orientation because aperture and resurfacing fail."

